  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KIGALI-HFC IMPLEMENTATION PLAN (KIP) PRP-UNDP-LBN-01002962</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Montreal Protocol aims to eliminate ozone-depleting substances (ODS), with financial and technical support provided to developing countries, including those under Article 5 (A-5), to facilitate this transition. The United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) assists these nations in implementing phase-out projects. Lebanon, having completed initial phases of its HCFC phase-out management plan (HPMP) and ratified the Kigali Amendment, is preparing for Stage I of its Kigali Implementation Plan</narrative>
  </description>
